After reverting 4ad3984c8b725ef59856d174d09d1209d65933fc I built 4.0.21.Final-SNAPSHOT and everything works again.

ChannelInitializer:

``` java
        Bootstrap bootstrap = new Bootstrap();

        bootstrap.group(Stack.EVENT_LOOP)
                .channel(NioSocketChannel.class)
                .option(ChannelOption.ALLOCATOR, UnpooledByteBufAllocator.DEFAULT)
                .handler(new ChannelInitializer<SocketChannel>() {
                    @Override
                    protected void initChannel(SocketChannel channel) throws Exception {
                        channel.pipeline().addLast(new LoggingHandler("Client", LogLevel.TRACE));
                        channel.pipeline().addLast(new UaTcpClientAcknowledgeHandler(client, handshake));
                    }
                });
```

Although things are a bit more complicated than that because the acknowledge handler later gets removed and other handlers get added.

issue.body:
In Netty 4.0.20.Final

``` java
public class LEIntEncoder extends MessageToByteEncoder<Integer> {
    @Override
    protected void encode(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Integer msg, ByteBuf out) throws Exception {
        out.order(ByteOrder.LITTLE_ENDIAN).writeInt(msg);
    }
}
```

``` java
EmbeddedChannel channel = new EmbeddedChannel(new LEIntEncoder());

channel.writeOutbound(0x12345678);

System.out.println(ByteBufUtil.hexDump((ByteBuf) channel.readOutbound()));
```

Expected output is `78563412`, but was `00000000`.

JDK 8u5
Windows 7,8 and OSX 10.9.3
